{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"5113ef329fd541ee","type":"text","text":"`initializeAuditProcessor`","x":-535,"y":-402,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1c358a70e0a63379","type":"text","text":"`akocloud-micros/src/micros/backlog.perte/bl-lib/services/AuditProcessor.ts`\n","x":-567,"y":-680,"width":314,"height":128},
		{"id":"e67e8263d62b372c","type":"text","text":"si status = pending & param_lic_sys_state =  2 = 2","x":117,"y":-666,"width":317,"height":100},
		{"id":"e25220e269e3b062","type":"text","text":"### 2. \"Esperar\" la respuesta (polling pasivo)\n\nEl sistema **no espera activamente**. Lo que hace es un mecanismo de **reintento por piggyback**:\n\nCada vez que el dispositivo envía **cualquier mensaje** (sample, sync, status, etc.), entra por\n\n`handleInput`\n\n(línea 55). Si el mensaje **NO es** un\n\n`CMD_ACK`\n\nni\n\n`PARAM_ACK`\n\n, el código en las líneas 134-152 se ejecuta:","x":2456,"y":234,"width":364,"height":206},
		{"id":"3f85b9f358e97217","type":"text","text":"Device envía un sample/sync/status/etc.\n  → AMQP: \"driver.input.perte\"  \n    → translator.perte :: handleInput()\n      → Procesa el mensaje normalmente\n      → ADEMÁS, busca pending: getPendingOutputMessage()\n        → Si hay PENDING → reenvía el comando al device\n        → updateRetries() incrementa contador\n          → Si max_retries → emite \"12830.output.failed\" y cancela\n          → Si no → sendEvent(\"cl.output.perte.coap.driver\", outputMsg)","x":2989,"y":268,"width":391,"height":252},
		{"id":"9d28fe1a485511dc","type":"text","text":"### 3. Confirmación (Device → Translator)\n\nCuando el dispositivo **aplica** los cambios, envía un `cmd_ack`\n\n```js\n{ \"id\": [974130021, 6000, 1, 26, 0], \"ty\": \"cmd_ack\", \"bid\": 12345 }\n```\n\nEsto entra por\n\n`handleInput`\n\n(líneas 108-122):","x":3604,"y":306,"width":476,"height":234},
		{"id":"650f7dc8d086588d","type":"text","text":"\n![[Pasted image 20260311103914.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20260311103848.png]]","x":3720,"y":-280,"width":516,"height":358},
		{"id":"6d0135275a88af1e","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20260311103403.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20260311103427.png]]","x":2860,"y":-391,"width":449,"height":222},
		{"id":"09e39d27f46825be","type":"text","text":"![[Pasted image 20260311110411.png]]\n\n![[Pasted image 20260311113603.png]]","x":3124,"y":-18,"width":516,"height":218},
		{"id":"5e86b2188319042c","type":"text","text":"### 1. `PENDING` — API envía configuración\n\nAPI → backlog.mediator → statecontroller.handleNewConfiguration()\n  → Crea/actualiza documento en `backlogs` con status: \"pending\"\n  → Envía al translator → translator crea `outputMsg` PENDING\n  → Envía CoAP al dispositivo","x":1376,"y":841,"width":504,"height":279},
		{"id":"de4d9c28c6863f61","type":"text","text":"### 2. `SEND` — Dispositivo recibe y envía `cmd_ack`\n\nADevice envía cmd_ack → translator.handleInput()\n  → outputMsgService.confirmOutput() → outputMsg: CONFIRMED\n  → publishParsedData() → llega al statecontroller.handleConfirmation()\n    → backlogProcessor.processConfirmationMessage()\n      → Si bid != null → backlog status: \"pending\" → \"send\"\n      → Si bid == null → backlog status: \"pending\" → \"rejected\"\nEl `cmd_ack` confirma que el dispositivo **recibió** el comando, pero aún no confirma que lo **aplicó**.","x":2184,"y":841,"width":504,"height":279},
		{"id":"297109263e3f161f","type":"text","text":"### 3. `CONFIRMED` — Dispositivo envía `audit`\n\nDevice aplica el cambio → envía mensaje tipo \"audit\"\n  → translator parsea → statecontroller.handleAudit()\n    → auditProcessor.processAuditMessage() → crea audit en BD\n    → backlogProcessor.confirmAudit()\n      → Busca backlog con status \"send\"\n      → Compara ref + newValue del audit con los del backlog.config\n      → Si match → config item: \"confirmed\"\n      → Si TODOS los items confirmed → backlog status: \"confirmed\" ✅","x":2933,"y":841,"width":504,"height":279},
		{"id":"9ea66424de53af69","type":"text","text":"Entonces el **audit lo envía el dispositivo automáticamente** cuando aplica el cambio de parámetro. No lo mokeas tú — el dispositivo real, después de recibir el `cmd` y aplicarlo, genera un mensaje `ty: \"audit\"` informando del cambio.","x":3628,"y":917,"width":472,"height":203},
		{"id":"b94cf35ecf74e02b","type":"text","text":"Mensaje audit \n```sh\nnode bin/examples/client-perte.js 974130021 0x2E19CFDA300B3F385A343536754B33324B572E7E audit -pl '{\"id\":[974130021,6000,1,26,0],\"ty\":\"audit\",\"d\":[[1773220600,530,0,2,1,1]]}' -v\n```","x":4255,"y":888,"width":472,"height":203},
		{"id":"a2a0fb88862df9b4","type":"text","text":"[[AKO 44 - Flujo de cambio de parámetros Cloud - Device.canvas]]","x":-1800,"y":-552,"width":297,"height":78},
		{"id":"a06779c827f605ba","type":"text","text":"### 1. Primer envío (API → Device)\n\n*Cambio de configuración mediante *\n`api/src/controllers/api/configuration/send-amqp/endConfig12830`","x":-1651,"y":-185,"width":326,"height":171},
		{"id":"7b10b95462a4505b","type":"text","text":"***backlog.perte mediator***\n\nrecibe el mensaje de la API, lo valida y clasifica, y luego lo reenvía al statecontroller\n\n\n","x":-1240,"y":-185,"width":300,"height":171},
		{"id":"76eb3bf9c33fdd6d","type":"text","text":"\n\n***backlog.perte stateController***\n\n`handleNewConfiguration`\ncrea/actualiza el backlog en la BD:","x":-800,"y":-185,"width":300,"height":171},
		{"id":"070b60bd71e40b77","type":"text","text":"***backlog.perte stateController***\n\n`handleAudit`\nCuando llega el **audit**, lo confirma de `\"send\"` a `confirmed`\n\n.","x":-1240,"y":300,"width":300,"height":171},
		{"id":"ae92cc5faa4935c8","type":"text","text":"***backlog.perte stateController***\n\n`handleConfirmation`\nCuando llega Confirmación `cmd_ack` actualiza el backlog de `\"pending\"` a `\"send\"`:\n\n\n\n","x":-1240,"y":60,"width":300,"height":171},
		{"id":"f7aeb8ac2f7066e2","type":"text","text":"cmd_ack_error","x":815,"y":305,"width":145,"height":50},
		{"id":"67b10b69199e36aa","type":"text","text":"Ejemplo el dispositivo se queda sin cobertura y al recuperarla este ahora tiene otra ip y al reconectarse este lo primero que haria seria enviar los datos acumulados","x":1180,"y":354,"width":241,"height":197},
		{"id":"792ef8f7b927172b","type":"text","text":"Otros : Sample, Events ...","x":815,"y":423,"width":160,"height":58},
		{"id":"19345539d93a5f84","type":"text","text":"Script `client-perte`\n```js\nnode bin/examples/client-perte.js 974130021 <uuid> cmd_ack -v\n```","x":743,"y":95,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a9d2ceba91498e0e","type":"text","text":"Mensaje de Audit","x":515,"y":-425,"width":180,"height":60},
		{"id":"d4f2417d3f9f34a1","type":"text","text":"PendingOutput Anulado","x":823,"y":-425,"width":245,"height":60},
		{"id":"3ca9cd6e3e18b0af","type":"text","text":"Translator\n\n`handleOutput()`\n- Parsea el mensaje del backlog\n- Convierte los parámetros a formato CoAP (registros MODBUS del dispositivo)\n- Guarda en MongoDB con `storeOutput()` → crea documento en `outputMsg` con status `PENDING`\n- Envía** por primera vez: `sendEvent(\"cl.output.perte.coap.driver\", toCLMessage)` → esto baja al CL (Communication Layer) que envía por CoAP al dispositivo","x":-285,"y":-185,"width":285,"height":171},
		{"id":"b047fbf2d5cad9e6","type":"text","text":"CL","x":440,"y":-129,"width":140,"height":60},
